WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:02.082
- In the 1980s, he was homeless

00:00:02.082 --> 00:00:04.734
while he tried to raise his toddler son.

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:07.143
To get off the streets
he became a stockbroker

00:00:07.143 --> 00:00:08.760
and later an entrepreneur.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.577
Today, he is worth
millions and had Will Smith

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.869
play him in a movie.

00:00:12.869 --> 00:00:13.994
He's Chris Gardner

00:00:13.994 --> 00:00:17.494
and here are his top 10 rules for success.

00:00:20.016 --> 00:00:21.804
- You got to have a plan.

00:00:21.804 --> 00:00:22.996
Everybody's got a dream,

00:00:22.996 --> 00:00:24.540
everybody's got a goal.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.548
What's the plan?

00:00:26.548 --> 00:00:28.206
And your plan has got to have something

00:00:28.206 --> 00:00:30.452
I call the C5 complex.

00:00:30.452 --> 00:00:31.285
Your plan has got to be

00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:34.481
clear, concise, compelling,
consistent, and committed.

00:00:34.481 --> 00:00:36.102
You got to have a plan

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.350
and when you're trying to do something

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.980
that you are truly passionate about,

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:41.563
there is no Plan B.

00:00:42.614 --> 00:00:44.359
- Okay.
- Plan B sucks.

00:00:44.359 --> 00:00:45.192
- [Brendan] Alright.

00:00:45.192 --> 00:00:47.504
(audience laughing)

00:00:47.504 --> 00:00:48.337
Okay.

00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:49.378
So it's as simple as that.

00:00:49.378 --> 00:00:50.400
- You got to have a plan.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.766
I mean think about that for a second.

00:00:52.766 --> 00:00:54.931
Three examples, Michael Jordan,

00:00:54.931 --> 00:00:58.033
won six NBA championships
with the Chicago Bulls

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.440
because he was committed
to Plan A not Plan B.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.824
Oprah Winfrey became
the queen of all media

00:01:03.824 --> 00:01:07.572
because she was committed
to Plan A not Plan B.

00:01:07.572 --> 00:01:09.237
Whatever your politics are,

00:01:09.237 --> 00:01:11.868
Barack Obama is sitting in the White House

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:16.050
because he was committed
to Plan A, not Plan B.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.118
- [Brendan] Okay.

00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:18.368
- Plan B sucks.

00:01:19.652 --> 00:01:20.732
What worked for me

00:01:20.732 --> 00:01:24.849
regarding balance between family
and business opportunities

00:01:24.849 --> 00:01:27.532
was always to be mindful of

00:01:27.532 --> 00:01:29.949
in a tie, family comes first.

00:01:31.531 --> 00:01:34.131
My child always came first.

00:01:34.131 --> 00:01:37.469
If you've managed your
relationships properly

00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:40.435
the business presentation
you're so concerned about,

00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:42.150
the big conference call that cannot happen

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.195
without you on the phone.

00:01:44.195 --> 00:01:47.199
All those things can be rescheduled

00:01:47.199 --> 00:01:51.253
but your son is going to
have one first baseball game,

00:01:51.253 --> 00:01:54.324
your daughter's going to
have one first dance recital

00:01:54.324 --> 00:01:56.015
and you got to be there.

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.848
In a tie, family wins.

00:01:58.813 --> 00:02:01.297
I made up my mind as a young guy,

00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:05.405
I wanted to become
world-class at something.

00:02:05.405 --> 00:02:09.521
I just had to find out what
that something was going to be.

00:02:09.521 --> 00:02:11.430
And the very first time

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:14.260
that I walked into a
Wall Street trading room,

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.760
I knew this is it.

00:02:16.855 --> 00:02:18.390
The ticker tape is rolling,

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.747
the phones are ringin' off the hook,

00:02:19.747 --> 00:02:21.678
people are screaming
and shouting out orders,

00:02:21.678 --> 00:02:23.355
bodies are flying all over the place.

00:02:23.355 --> 00:02:26.600
And what looked like
chaos to anybody else,

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.583
I could see the natural rhythm in it.

00:02:29.583 --> 00:02:31.701
It was like I was reading a sheet of music

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:34.354
and I knew this is where
I'm supposed to be.

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.311
I kept coming back.

00:02:36.311 --> 00:02:39.255
I wore one branch manager down

00:02:39.255 --> 00:02:41.031
to the point that he says to me,

00:02:41.031 --> 00:02:43.401
"Gardner, based on persistence alone,

00:02:43.401 --> 00:02:45.671
"we going to give you a shot."

00:02:45.671 --> 00:02:46.857
Man, I quit my job.

00:02:46.857 --> 00:02:48.389
That was all I wanted.

00:02:48.389 --> 00:02:49.912
I went home and I told my ex,

00:02:49.912 --> 00:02:51.712
"You know what, you said I couldn't do it

00:02:51.712 --> 00:02:54.018
"but guess what, I start in two weeks."

00:02:54.018 --> 00:02:56.144
Too many of us for a long time

00:02:56.144 --> 00:02:59.706
have confused our net
worth and our self-worth.

00:02:59.706 --> 00:03:01.630
Your net worth is going to fluctuate.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:02.969
It's going to go up and down.

00:03:02.969 --> 00:03:04.833
That's what money does

00:03:04.833 --> 00:03:07.950
but your self-worth should not.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:08.886
Who you are,

00:03:08.886 --> 00:03:11.664
what's important to you, how you live,

00:03:11.664 --> 00:03:14.914
your values should never be negotiable,

00:03:16.104 --> 00:03:17.021
compromised

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.477
and you should never settle.

00:03:20.477 --> 00:03:22.695
Again, we have gotten to this point

00:03:22.695 --> 00:03:24.706
where we've got to say to ourselves,

00:03:24.706 --> 00:03:27.539
my net worth is not my self-worth.

00:03:29.413 --> 00:03:32.506
How you motivate key employees, I believe,

00:03:32.506 --> 00:03:33.673
is number one,

00:03:34.792 --> 00:03:36.480
you got to respect them.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.207
You got to let them grow

00:03:39.207 --> 00:03:42.793
and you got to trust
them and leave 'em alone.

00:03:42.793 --> 00:03:45.294
And you have to also
show them the opportunity

00:03:45.294 --> 00:03:47.908
to make more money than they've
ever made in their lives.

00:03:47.908 --> 00:03:49.677
All that combined,

00:03:49.677 --> 00:03:53.138
that's how you motivate
your key core employees.

00:03:53.138 --> 00:03:55.801
If you're looking to instigate
a change in your life,

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:59.410
there's no better or
worse time than right now.

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.332
Hey, I understand.

00:04:01.332 --> 00:04:02.564
Change is scary.

00:04:02.564 --> 00:04:04.113
With the status quo,

00:04:04.113 --> 00:04:05.663
you know what you've got.

00:04:05.663 --> 00:04:07.120
And you shake things up,

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.534
there's no telling what
you might end up with.

00:04:09.534 --> 00:04:12.414
But two other things
are true about change,

00:04:12.414 --> 00:04:16.280
one, it is absolutely
necessary for personal growth

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:18.977
and two, it's going to happen.

00:04:18.977 --> 00:04:20.375
Either you can pick the time

00:04:20.375 --> 00:04:22.501
to instigate the change you want

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:25.396
or the change and the time will pick you.

00:04:25.396 --> 00:04:27.788
So if you happen to be one of those people

00:04:27.788 --> 00:04:30.453
who's standing on the
sidelines of your dreams,

00:04:30.453 --> 00:04:32.606
waiting for that perfect moment.

00:04:32.606 --> 00:04:34.263
If you want to make that change

00:04:34.263 --> 00:04:36.434
but you just don't know if you're ready,

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:39.005
this life lesson is for you.

00:04:39.005 --> 00:04:43.322
It's time to stop digging
your potatoes and jump.

00:04:43.322 --> 00:04:45.862
Baby steps count too.

00:04:45.862 --> 00:04:48.110
As long as you're going forward

00:04:48.110 --> 00:04:50.283
and one day you add
all those baby steps up

00:04:50.283 --> 00:04:53.499
and you might be surprised
at where you can get to.

00:04:53.499 --> 00:04:54.698
But more importantly,

00:04:54.698 --> 00:04:57.320
I remember something my mom
used to say to me every day.

00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:01.170
She would say, "Son, the
calvary ain't comin'.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.475
"You got to do this yourself.

00:05:02.475 --> 00:05:04.703
"Ain't no backup.

00:05:04.703 --> 00:05:05.568
"Okay?"

00:05:05.568 --> 00:05:09.202
And when you put those
two things together, man.

00:05:09.202 --> 00:05:11.216
It wasn't as hard to keep going forward

00:05:11.216 --> 00:05:12.791
as you might think.

00:05:12.791 --> 00:05:14.057
Well now that we can see

00:05:14.057 --> 00:05:17.008
how short life really can be,

00:05:17.008 --> 00:05:21.563
what are you going to do
with the rest of your life?

00:05:21.563 --> 00:05:23.146
That's the trigger.

00:05:24.733 --> 00:05:28.083
That's the biggest trigger
that I have ever experienced.

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:31.750
What are you going to do
the rest of your life?

00:05:33.564 --> 00:05:35.956
And what I had to do

00:05:35.956 --> 00:05:40.051
was I had to start taking
some of my own advice.

00:05:40.051 --> 00:05:41.426
I had been telling people,

00:05:41.426 --> 00:05:44.052
I had written about it
for a very long time

00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:45.327
that if you're doing something

00:05:45.327 --> 00:05:47.572
that you're not totally committed to,

00:05:47.572 --> 00:05:48.426
if you're doing something

00:05:48.426 --> 00:05:50.724
that you're not totally passionate about,

00:05:50.724 --> 00:05:54.111
you're compromising yourself every day.

00:05:54.111 --> 00:05:58.691
I was presentable but I
wore the same two suits.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:00.806
I had two suits, man.

00:06:00.806 --> 00:06:04.306
That I had to wear everyday for a year.

00:06:04.306 --> 00:06:05.889
One blue, one gray.

00:06:06.867 --> 00:06:08.950
The joke around the office started,

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.106
"Oh, that's Chris Gardner.

00:06:10.106 --> 00:06:12.214
"He's reenacting the Civil War."

00:06:12.214 --> 00:06:13.986
(audience laughing)

00:06:13.986 --> 00:06:17.178
Some days with the north,
some days he's with the south.

00:06:17.178 --> 00:06:19.501
(audience laughing)

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:22.715
I'll never forget a recent experience,

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.886
doing my business on Wall Street,

00:06:24.886 --> 00:06:26.997
getting on the train to
come back to Midtown,

00:06:26.997 --> 00:06:29.170
one o'clock in the afternoon.

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:32.350
Normally there's a low,
this train should be empty.

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.267
But on this day the train was full,

00:06:36.992 --> 00:06:40.796
full of people all in business suits.

00:06:40.796 --> 00:06:42.254
A guy recognizes me,

00:06:42.254 --> 00:06:45.383
comes over and says, "Hey,
are you Chris Gardner?"

00:06:45.383 --> 00:06:46.966
We started talking.

00:06:47.838 --> 00:06:51.327
Turns out I'm in the
car with the first wave

00:06:51.327 --> 00:06:55.494
of the 55,000 people who had
just been laid off by Citibank

00:06:57.097 --> 00:06:58.804
and I noticed something.

00:06:58.804 --> 00:07:01.291
Everyone was holding a box.

00:07:01.291 --> 00:07:02.213
You've seen the boxes,

00:07:02.213 --> 00:07:03.746
you've seen them on television.

00:07:03.746 --> 00:07:05.899
They've got their
houseplant, their coffee mug,

00:07:05.899 --> 00:07:07.937
the pictures of their kids.

00:07:07.937 --> 00:07:09.957
And they're all going home.

00:07:09.957 --> 00:07:12.677
They're all going home to tell their wife,

00:07:12.677 --> 00:07:16.226
their husband, their
children, and the landlord

00:07:16.226 --> 00:07:18.059
they don't have a job.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:21.620
I began to share with this young guy that,

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.383
"Well you know what,

00:07:23.383 --> 00:07:25.223
yeah, you lost your job

00:07:25.223 --> 00:07:27.116
but you haven't lost your skills,

00:07:27.116 --> 00:07:29.087
your talent, or your expertise.

00:07:29.087 --> 00:07:30.635
What we've got to do now

00:07:30.635 --> 00:07:32.483
is create opportunities where the skill,

00:07:32.483 --> 00:07:35.900
talent and expertise can be transferable.

00:07:36.839 --> 00:07:39.584
Creating an opportunity
and looking for a job

00:07:39.584 --> 00:07:41.269
are two different things.

00:07:41.269 --> 00:07:46.101
This could be prime time
for pushing your button

00:07:46.101 --> 00:07:48.261
rather finding your button.

00:07:48.261 --> 00:07:49.947
What do I mean by that?

00:07:49.947 --> 00:07:52.617
Prime time to find that one thing

00:07:52.617 --> 00:07:54.725
that you love to do so much,

00:07:54.725 --> 00:07:57.552
you would get up in the
morning and do it free.

00:07:57.552 --> 00:07:59.838
Prime time to find that one thing

00:07:59.838 --> 00:08:00.982
that the sun cannot,

00:08:00.982 --> 00:08:02.907
comes up soon enough in the morning

00:08:02.907 --> 00:08:05.856
because you want to go do your thing.

00:08:05.856 --> 00:08:09.277
This could be that time in your life.

00:08:09.277 --> 00:08:10.790
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:14.411
I made this video because
Arsh Solutions asked me to.

00:08:14.411 --> 00:08:15.607
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:08:15.607 --> 00:08:17.433
that you want me to profile next,

00:08:17.433 --> 00:08:18.773
leave it in the comments below

00:08:18.773 --> 00:08:21.023
and I'll see what I can do.

